{"title":"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(extremely_simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (extremely simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Also_very_simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Also very simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/83357600a32dc213f800922786ff07c27be954f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GHIJ$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> are equal in area. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoints of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/798a1cea398f29087ec5d72ff1bfef89d52ee835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IH$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/7381d73a5fd25fe335bba4cd0b2219adaf09ed3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HE$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, respectively. What is the ratio of the area of the shaded pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f44f7fd1eb74392be12c584465a560156e820d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJICB$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> to the sum of the areas of the three squares?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b2b73722908630bee557f37fc8e4a5e91966797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{7}{24}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{3}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\hspace{.05in}\\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"388\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169139bda69e81f8342f246f95cc3f636c1f9abe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J;  A = (0.5,2); B = (1.5,2); C = (1.5,1); D = (0.5,1); E = (0,1); F = (0,0); G = (1,0); H = (1,1); I = (2,1); J = (2,0);  draw(A--B);  draw(C--B);  draw(D--A);   draw(F--E);  draw(I--J);  draw(J--F);  draw(G--H);  draw(A--J);  filldraw(A--B--C--I--J--cycle,grey); draw(E--I); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NW); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NE); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NW); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, NW); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, SW); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, S); dot(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, N); dot(&quot;$I$&quot;, I, NE); dot(&quot;$J$&quot;, J, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let point X be the point that intersects line EI. We can split  our original triangle into trapezoid ABCX and triangle XIJ. WLOG (Without Loss Of Generality),  AB equals 1 unit. Then since, X is the midpoint of line AJ, and point A is 1.5 units horizontally from J, the midpoint X will be 0.75 units away horizontally from A  and thus 0.25 units horizontally from C. Therefore XC equals 0.25 units. Using the area formulas for trapezoids and triangles, we calculate the area of ABCX to be 0.625 and XIJ to be 0.375. The combined areas (which are equivalent to our original triangle)  equal 1. Therefore, the ratio of the area of the hexagon to the three squares is 1:3 because the area of the three squares is 3. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60f3a6d0a96f2d2661058caddb24ee044da6a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac {1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />-~TheNerdwhoIsNerdy. \n</p><p>Edits for Clarity and Accuracy by RamanujanIsBetter\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28extremely_simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(extremely_simple)\">Solution 2 (extremely simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (extremely simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend line AD such that it intersects line FG. Call the intersection K. If we assign an arbitrary value to the side lengths of the squares, such as 2, the base of the now formed triangle AJK would have a length of 3, while the height would be 4. The area of triangle AJK would then be 6, and the rectangle EDKF would have an area of 2. 6 + 2 = 8, and since all of the squares' areas add up to a total of 12 (if each has side length 2), we obtain (12 - 8)/12 for the shaded part of the diagram which yields 4/12 = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60f3a6d0a96f2d2661058caddb24ee044da6a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac {1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~ martianrunner\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Also_very_simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Also_very_simple)\">Solution 3 (Also very simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Also very simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Name the intersection of line segment AJ and CH as K. Notice that triangle ADK is congruent to triangle JIK by AAS (Angle-Angle-Side), so they have the same area. Therefore, the shaded area is just the area of the topmost square which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60f3a6d0a96f2d2661058caddb24ee044da6a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac {1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" /> of the whole.\n</p><p>~ Brainwhizz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8\">2013 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php